%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: YuriIntermission
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988699465252940
    - rid: 4927988699465252942
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Hmm... Let's see here...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988699465252943
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri is looking through her journal on Mysticism, the one Mirabelle gave
      her.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"The act of Marking, as the name implies, requires leaving an impression
      on the Mundus."'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"There are several ways to do this; however, recent innovations in marking
      involve an ''aetherial'' mark."'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"This is generally preferable to the primitive marks of the past, which
      relied on imprinting physical locations onto the soul of the user."'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"Naturally, imprinting physical coordinates onto a soul requires far
      more concentration and effort than placing the imprint on the world."'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"This does mean that aetherial markings are more ephemeral than their
      physical counterparts; they disappear after a successful recall."'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"The best of both worlds can be found through enchanting, which uses
      the soul energy imbued in the chosen item to maintain the aetherial mark."'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708800
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"These enchanted objects require concentration to use..."'
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708801
    - rid: 4927988726549708807
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: '"... <b>always use both hands whenever you place a mark</b>?"'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708802
    - rid: 4927988726549708804
    - rid: 4927988726549708806
    - rid: 4927988726549708808
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 15749674ba4a7a9428fe9cc574046344, type: 2}
    dialog: If that note is in there, it is probably because it is true.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708809
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: That doesn't answer the question of why, though...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708810
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 15749674ba4a7a9428fe9cc574046344, type: 2}
    dialog: This one understands that you are new to magic-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708813
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 15749674ba4a7a9428fe9cc574046344, type: 2}
    dialog: Writing down what not to do in your notes is a right of passage.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708811
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: I see...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708812
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 15749674ba4a7a9428fe9cc574046344, type: 2}
    dialog: Now quit stalling, show off this teleportation spell!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708814
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah- right.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708815
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri casts the Mark spell (with both of her hands, of course).
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708816
    - rid: 4927988726549708817
    - rid: 4927988726549708818
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: The aetherial energy appears to have coalesced, so I should be able to
      cast the Recall.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708819
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Yuri leaves the Arcanaeum, so she can demonstrate her teleportation.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708820
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 15749674ba4a7a9428fe9cc574046344, type: 2}
    dialog: Impressive! It worked, it worked!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708821
    - rid: 4927988726549708822
    - rid: 4927988726549708823
    - rid: 4927988726549708825
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Haaaahh... haaaahh...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: The notes left out the part where recalling would be so draining...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708826
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 15749674ba4a7a9428fe9cc574046344, type: 2}
    dialog: At even such a short distance?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 15749674ba4a7a9428fe9cc574046344, type: 2}
    dialog: You need to practice more, my friend.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988726549708827
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: You're probably right...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
